FAQ = [
 ("What is the best trailer hitch for a 2022+ Jeep Grand Cherokee?",
  "For most owners, the Draw-Tite 76595. It is rated 7,500 lb gross trailer weight and 1,125 lb tongue weight, with the same figures under weight distribution, so it covers even the 7,200 lb V8 rating. It fits the 2022–2026 two-row and the 2021–2026 Grand Cherokee L, and Draw-Tite quotes a 90-minute install with no drilling. The CURT 13525 is the close alternative, but it excludes the two-row Trailhawk."),
 ("How much can the 2022+ Grand Cherokee tow?",
  "Dealer towing guides list 6,200 lb for the 3.6L V6, 7,200 lb for the 5.7L V8 where it was offered, and 6,000 lb for the 4xe on Trailhawk and higher trims, with base 4xe trims at 3,500 lb. Wikipedia lists slightly different V6 figures, so the owner's manual towing chart for your VIN is the number to trust. The hitch rating never raises the vehicle rating."),
 ("Do 2011–2021 Grand Cherokee hitches fit the 2022 model?",
  "Only if your 2022 is the carry-over WK body. For 2022, Jeep sold the new WL alongside the old model, badged Grand Cherokee WK. Hitches like the Draw-Tite 75699 list \"2011–2021 Grand Cherokee, 2022 Grand Cherokee WK\" and will not fit a WL. If your 2022 has the new body, it's a WL and needs a 2022+ part such as the 76595 or CURT 13525."),
 ("Does the Grand Cherokee L use the same hitch?",
  "The aftermarket hitches here are sold as one part for both: the Draw-Tite 76595 and CURT 13525 each list the 2022–2026 Grand Cherokee and 2021–2026 Grand Cherokee L. Mopar uses separate receivers: 82219040AA for the two-row and 82219041AA for the three-row L. The L launched a year earlier, for 2021, and was never offered as a Trailhawk."),
 ("Does my Grand Cherokee already have a hitch?",
  "Check under the rear fascia for a square receiver. Dealer guides describe the available tow package as including a Class IV receiver and 4- and 7-pin wiring, so a tow-package vehicle already has what you need except a ball mount. Mopar's replacement listing describes the production receiver as a Class III, 2 in part, so check the label on yours for its rating. If there is no receiver, any hitch here bolts on."),
 ("Will these hitches fit the Grand Cherokee 4xe?",
  "The Draw-Tite 76595 lists the 2022–2026 Grand Cherokee with no trim exclusion. CURT's 13525 excludes the two-row Trailhawk. Since the Trailhawk and 4xe overlap, 4xe Trailhawk owners should use the Draw-Tite or Mopar part and confirm fit with the seller. Tow ratings on the 4xe are lower than the V8: 6,000 lb on Trailhawk and higher trims, 3,500 lb on base 4xe trims per dealer guides."),
 ("Do I have to remove the rear fascia to install a hitch?",
  "Partly, for the concealed designs. CURT says the 13525 requires removal of rear quarter panels and the bumper covering because the main body sits hidden behind the fascia. Draw-Tite quotes 90 minutes for the 76595 with no drilling. Plan on a couple of hours, plastic trim tools, and a helper to hold the 41–42 lb hitch while you start the bolts."),
 ("What wiring do I need to tow with a Grand Cherokee?",
  "A 4-way flat connector covers lights on small trailers. For a camper or boat with electric brakes you need a 7-way connector and a brake controller. Dealer guides say the factory tow package includes both 4- and 7-pin wiring. If you are adding a hitch to a vehicle without the package, add the harness to the same order."),
 ("Is a 7,500 lb hitch overkill on a Grand Cherokee?",
  "No, and it is common. The Draw-Tite 76595 and CURT 13525 are rated 7,500 lb because they are built for the heaviest configuration, the 7,200 lb V8. On a 6,200 lb V6 or 6,000 lb 4xe, the extra hitch capacity doesn't let you tow more, but it adds margin, and the high tongue ratings (1,125 lb on the Draw-Tite) suit heavy bike racks."),
 ("Can I use weight distribution on a Grand Cherokee?",
  "Both brand-name hitches here are rated for weight distribution: 7,500 lb and 1,125 lb on the Draw-Tite 76595, and 7,500 lb and 750 lb on the CURT 13525. Whether Jeep requires or allows weight distribution on your vehicle is set by the owner's manual, so check its towing section before fitting a WD hitch, especially on air-suspension trims."),
]

